{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1910 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "c7be1122fc287dc1dd54f4ed93d912eec4094a36b685bf994405976667be313e" :edb/db-before-t 1909 :edb/db-after-t 1910 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535222 50 #inst "2026-10-08T19:53:26.935Z" 13194139535222 true] [17592186179523 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x$, where $C=C_1 \\cup C_2$ is the path comprising of two line segments, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3708/Source/Images/8e812447b89c4e3aa73cf9f3313ab5fc.png)" 13194139535222 false] [17592186179523 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x,$ where $C=C_1 \\cup C_2$ is the path comprising of two line segments, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/3d408de0d50e2688aa0b35d8af39b6847cfdf21d5ec583320f0204384304fbc8.png)" 13194139535222 true] [17592186179523 1145 "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1\n$$\n\nwhere $x_2$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $x_1$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $x_2 = -3$ and $x_1 = 3$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1 = (-3) - 3 = -6\n$$" 13194139535222 false] [17592186179523 1145 "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_2$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $x_1$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $x_2 = -3$ and $x_1 = 3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1 = (-3) - 3 = -6.\n$$" 13194139535222 true] [17592186179524 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y$, where $C$ is the path along the semicircle of radius $3$, traversed from the point $(3,0)$ to the point $(-3,0)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3708/Source/Images/57e461e49aa9411e4aeb899975abcd92.png)" 13194139535222 false] [17592186179524 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y,$ where $C$ is the path along the semicircle of radius $3,$ traversed from the point $(3,0)$ to the point $(-3,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/ca97546ecaf9e37bee53fcc2b0c66962cff67a91ee9b117cc8ac8531efa23efc.png)" 13194139535222 true] [17592186179524 1145 "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1\n$$\n\nwhere $y_2$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $y_1$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $y_2 = 0$ and $y_1 = 0$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1 = 0 - 0 = 0\n$$" 13194139535222 false] [17592186179524 1145 "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1,\n$$\n\nwhere $y_2$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $y_1$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $y_2 = 0$ and $y_1 = 0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1 =  0 - 0 = 0.\n$$" 13194139535222 true] [17592186179525 1100 "If $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= 8$ and $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= -2$, calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x$ given that $C = C_1\\cup C_2$." 13194139535222 false] [17592186179525 1100 "If $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= 8$ and $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= -2,$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x$ given that $C = C_1\\cup C_2.$" 13194139535222 true] [17592186179525 1145 "Let\n\n$$\nC = C_1\\cup C_2\n$$\n\nbe a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation.\n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x$, we have the following properties:\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = -\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = \\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x + \\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{C}f(x, y)dx &= ∫_{C_{1}}f(x, y)dx + ∫_{C_{2}}f(x, y)dx \\\\\n8 &= - ∫_{-C_{1}}f(x, y)dx - ∫_{-C_{2}}f(x, y)dx \\\\\n8 &= - (-2) - ∫_{-C_{2}}f(x, y)dx \\\\\n8 &= 2 - ∫_{-C_{2}}f(x, y)dx \\\\\n6 &= - ∫_{-C_{2}}f(x, y)dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x = -6\n$$" 13194139535222 false] [17592186179525 1145 "Let $C = C_1\\cup C_2$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = -\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = \\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x + \\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =-(-2)-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =2-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x = -6.\n$$" 13194139535222 true] [17592186179661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338349 13194139535222 true] [17592186179661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338356 13194139535222 true] [17592186179661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338363 13194139535222 true] [17592186179662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338370 13194139535222 true] [17592186179662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338377 13194139535222 true] [17592186179662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338384 13194139535222 true] [17592186179662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338391 13194139535222 true] [17592186179663 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338321 13194139535222 true] [17592186179663 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338328 13194139535222 true] [17592186179663 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338335 13194139535222 true] [17592186179663 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338342 13194139535222 true] [17592186179930 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535222 true] [17592186179930 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/ac639fb08d54d2004aec96708ffd19bc080b028e739075687a84a09158cd4fd2.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along a semicircle of radius $2,$ traversed from the point $(2,1)$ to the point $(-2,1),$ shown above." 13194139535222 true] [17592186179930 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3708/Source/Images/q-124146.png)\n\nCalculate $∫_{C}dx$, where $C$ is the path along a semicircle of radius $2$, traversed from the point $(2, 1)$ to the point $(-2, 1)$, shown above." 13194139535222 false] [17592186179930 1145 "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=-2$ and ${x}_{1}=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=(-2)-2=-4.\n$$" 13194139535222 true] [17592186179931 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535222 true] [17592186179931 1100 "Calculate ${∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the closed path along the unit circle, traversed once in the counterclockwise direction." 13194139535222 true] [17592186179931 1100 "Calculate $∮_{C}dx$, where $C$ is the closed path along the unit circle, traversed once in the counterclockwise direction." 13194139535222 false] [17592186179931 1145 "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, the initial and terminal points are the same (since the path is closed and is traversed only once). Therefore, ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$" 13194139535222 true] [17592186179932 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535222 true] [17592186179932 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/2400f92070b4f7d4e0ad0309574b729da86754bc64b6d7a3c508433d1bbc7f76.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment between the points $(4,0)$ to the point $(0,3),$ as shown above." 13194139535222 true] [17592186179932 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3708/Source/Images/q-124148.png)\n\nCalculate $∫_{C}dy$, where $C$ is the path along the line segment between the points $(4, 0)$ to the point $(0, 3)$, as shown above." 13194139535222 false] [17592186179932 1145 "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{2}=3$ and ${y}_{1}=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=3-0=3.\n$$" 13194139535222 true] [17592186179933 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535222 true] [17592186179933 1100 "If ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=4$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=6,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" 13194139535222 true] [17592186179933 1100 "If $∫_{C_{1}}f(x, y)dx = 4$ and $∫_{-C_{2}}f(x, y)dx = 6$, calculate $∫_{C}f(x, y)dx$ given that $C = C_{1}∪C_{2}$." 13194139535222 false] [17592186179933 1145 "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4-6 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338321 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338322 13194139535222 true] [17592186338321 1089 "q-124179" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338321 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535222 true] [17592186338321 1100 "If ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=3$ and ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=5,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338321 1113 #uuid "91767182-155c-5640-b85b-b94d940de243" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338321 1145 "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-3+5 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338323 13194139535222 true] [17592186338322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338324 13194139535222 true] [17592186338322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338325 13194139535222 true] [17592186338322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338326 13194139535222 true] [17592186338322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338327 13194139535222 true] [17592186338322 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535222 true] [17592186338322 1041 "selection" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338322 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338326 13194139535222 true] [17592186338322 1110 #uuid "8d8443e6-8d4d-5286-89ef-37939581c384" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338323 1034 "Impossible to determine" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338323 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535222 true] [17592186338323 1111 #uuid "415ade7c-5a79-5492-8a50-edeb6668ef2d" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338324 1034 "8" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338324 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535222 true] [17592186338324 1111 #uuid "6c8ea61d-2dbd-596b-b490-02cd5e36e379" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338325 1034 "7" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338325 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535222 true] [17592186338325 1111 #uuid "124f71fe-c3d9-5275-a02a-e7bffd254773" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338326 1034 "2" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338326 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535222 true] [17592186338326 1111 #uuid "36787f21-988e-5c12-adf1-a110a30b1108" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338327 1034 "-2" 13194139535222 true] [17592186338327 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535222 true] [17592186338327 1111 #uuid "517cd13b-7e